-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",353,{
[11265]="7001B3F6\n1\tInform Candaith that you have arrived\tCandaith has been preparing the defences on the peak of Weathertop. Speak with him to confirm the plan for defeating the impending assault.\n2\tPush back the first assault\tThe first assault has begun. The Enemy will stop at nothing to destroy Candaith and reclaim what they lost.\n3\tPush back the second assault\tThe second assault has begun. Dark and powerful forces are at play.\n4\tPush back the third assault\tThe third assault has begun. The Enemy's power is waning under the strain of sustaining this unnatural attack.\n5\tDefeat the Cargûl\tThe leader of the Enemy's forces and architect of this attack has finally made his appearance on the battlefield. Defeat this servant of the Nine.\n",
[11266]="70029FC3\n1\tComplete 'Stand at Amon Sûl' in a raid group\tServants of the Witch-king have been drawn to Weathertop following a confrontation between the Nazgûl and the Wizard Gandalf the Grey. The Ranger Candaith has laid a trap to defeat the Cargûl who leads the dark forces to the ruins of Amon Sûl.\n",
[11267]="7001B76C\n1\tStand at Ost Galadh\t\n",
[11268]="7003E043\n1\tCollect uncommon ore (total: 8)\tCollect uncommon ore found within Stangraf for Quickbeam.\n",
[11269]="7003953A\n1\tDefeat the leader of the invaders in Stangraf\tEliminate the leader of the forces of Isengard within Stangraf.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam\tYou should return to Quickbeam and inform him of your success within Stangraf. Quickbeam can be found at Derndingle.\n",
[11270]="7003955C\n1\tDefeat invaders in Stangraf (total: 20)\tStangraf has acquired new residents since the mine was evacuated. The new squatters need to be evicted to prevent the enemy from taking the resources within.\n",
[11271]="7002C9E8\n1\tHelp Stanric and Gadda to take a stand\tGadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda.\n2\tTalk to Gadda\tGadda is outside of the Mead Hall in Stangard. You should speak with Gadda.\n",
[11272]="70019171\n1\tCollect chalk (total: 5)\030Collect red berries (total: 6)\tMenassiel in Cerin Amroth wishes you to collect chalk and red berries, to create the stark colours that help make Elven art so striking. Chalk can be chipped from white rocks to the north. Gather red berries from the bushes that can be found in the forests to the west.\n2\tBring the materials back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth\tHaving collected the raw materials for red and white pigments, you should bring them back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth.\n",
[11273]="70019172\n1\tCollect chalk (total: 5)\030Collect red berries (total: 6)\tMenassiel in Cerin Amroth wishes you to collect chalk and red berries, to create the stark colours that help make Elven art so striking. Chalk can be chipped from white rocks to the north. Gather red berries from the bushes that can be found in the forests to the west.\n2\tBring the materials back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth\tHaving collected the raw materials for red and white pigments, you should bring them back to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth.\n",
[11274]="7001AACF\n1\tTalk to Agorin to travel to Minas Gîl\tThe sorcerer responsible for the corruption of Minas Gîl may be found atop the pinnacle of that tower. Agorin has instructed you to gather allies and defeat the sorcerer responsible for the corruption of Minas Gîl and put an end to his sorcery.\n2\tTalk to Agorin at Ost Galadh\tAgorin is at Ost Galadh. You should return to Ost Galadh with news of your victory.\n",
[11275]="700439FE\n1\tTalk to Rock\tBy completing this quest, you will receive a Stars of Merit allowance.\n",
[11276]="70041175\n1\tSteal bags of rations from Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (total: 6)\tBags of rations can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially near Corsair tents. You have found bags of rations that might be of aid to the people of Gondor and should take them from the Corsairs.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have recovered many bags of rations in Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[11277]="7003566F\n1\tExamine goats (total: 6)\tGoats can be found in the hills of the western High Knolls. You should examine the goats.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have examined many starved goats in the western hills of the High Knolls. The signs of an epic struggle to survive are apparent all over Wildermore.\n",
[11278]="70052B22\n1\tDestroy spoiled provisions at Fil Sulmog (total: 8)\tSpoiled provisions can be found throughout Fil Sulmog. You have discovered the spoiled provisions of which Hárskor spoke, and you should now destroy them.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many spoiled provisions at Fil Sulmog.\n",
[11279]="70068345\n1\tAssist Khânai with the spice flow into Umbar Baharbêl\030Help Luthana meet epicurean desires\030Help Tevurin achieve his personal hunting goal\030Help Abido achieve his hunting dream\tDelona asked you to work with the various hunters and experts within the expedition camp to meet the needs of the craftspeople in Umbar city.\n2\tSpeak with Delona\tYou completed several tasks for the various hunters and experts within the expedition camp. Return to the expedition leader, Delona, and inform her of your efforts.\n",
[11280]="7000EB74\n1\tScout Tírith Rhaw\030Scout the Isendeep\tTírith Rhaw lies to the south-east of Gramsfoot and the Isendeep lies to the east. Forzunk instructed you to scout the Isendeep and Tírith Rhaw.\n2\tTalk to Forzunk at Gramsfoot\tForzunk is at Gramsfoot. You should report to Forzunk at once.\n",
[11281]="700082B5\n1\tDefeat Hillmen armourers\tThe Hillmen armourers are encamped south-east of the Ram Dúath. You should defeat the armourers before they can craft any more weapons for the Rauta-lehmä.\n2\tDefeat Hillmen armourers (total: 3)\tThe Hillmen armourers are encamped south-east of the Ram Dúath. You should defeat the amourers before they can craft any more weapons for the Rauta-lehmä.\n3\tCompleted\tYou succeeded in defeating the Hillmen armourers from Angmar who came to strengthen the Rauta-lehmä.\n",
[11282]="7000E39B\n1\tTalk to Eija\tEija is in Kauppa-kohta, at the lakeshore. Mainio suggested you speak with his mother, Eija, to learn if she could use your help.\n",
[11283]="7006B6C5\n1\tRepair barricades (total: 6)\tNingêna has asked you to repair the barricades protecting Sûru.\n2\tTalk to Ningêna\tYou have repaired the barricades protecting Sûru. You should return to Ningêna.\n",
[11284]="7002D3C3\n1\tReclaim the stolen coins of the dwarves (total: 8)\tThe goblin-thieves can be found in Snaga-maudhûl, in the western area of the Great Delving. You should reclaim the coins of dwarf-travellers that have been stolen by the waylaying goblins.\n2\tBring the coins you recovered to Wegil\tWegil can be found on the north-east side of Snaga-maudhûl in the Great Delving. You should bring the coins you recovered to Wegil.\n",
[11285]="700686A8\n1\tRecover stolen goods from the Heirsworn (total: 16)\tStolen goods can be found on ships crewed by Heirsworn Corsairs in the Sail-haven. Eshmun has asked you to recover goods stolen from Umbari merchants and from the markets of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver the stolen goods to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You have recovered many of the goods stolen by the Heirsworn in the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.\n",
[11286]="70040ED8\n1\tRetrieve stolen relics from Corsairs in Edhellond (total: 8)\tCorsairs of Umbar can be found throughout Edhellond in north-western Belfalas. Dolvir has asked you to recover any Elvish relics you can find from the raiding Corsairs in Belfalas.\n2\tTalk to Dolvir\tDolvir can be found on a hilltop to the east of Edhellond. You have recovered many stolen Elvish relics, and should now return them to Dolvir.\n",
[11287]="70002D06\n1\tBring food-stores to Ekhagan\030Collect food-stores (total: 8)\tFood-stores are kept within the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Ekhagan has asked you to steal food-stores from the city of Donnvail, where they are being kept for the use of the army of Angmar, so he can distribute them to the hungry people of his tribe.\n",
[11288]="7003FE60\n1\tDefeat slavers (total: 4)\tThe craftsmen must be rescued before the corsairs ship them off.\n",
[11289]="70027441\n1\tQuestion the first looter\030Question the second looter\030Question the third looter\030Question the fourth looter\030Question the fifth looter\tLooters can be found stealing stores throughout the Herd-lands. You should attempt to question looters on the farm, for they are generally more neutral than the Dragon-clan raiders.\n2\tReturn to Blodwen with the information\tBlodwen can be found hiding among the rocks at the southern end of the Herd-lands. You should bring the map you uncovered to Blodwen before you hurry back to Lhan Tarren.\n",
[11290]="70030886\n1\tCollect wood in Nîn-stazg (total: 6)\tOrcs build siege-weapons in the forest south-east of Floodwend. You should gather wood from the encampment where the Orcs have been chopping down trees.\n2\tCompleted\tThe supplies you captured from the Orcs will be put to far better use in the hands of Floodwend's people. You did well to retrieve the wood stockpiles from the grip of Mordor.\n",
[11291]="7005A674\n1\tDefeat Zaugnakh\030Defeat Mangáth\030Defeat Grámoz\030Defeat Ogarbur\tWarg champions can be found in eastern Azanulbizar. Valdi has asked you to defeat Warg champions.\n2\tReturn to Valdi\tValdi can be found in Amdân. You should talk to Valdi.\n",
[11292]="7001E7E9\n1\tTalk to Faerchiril at Barad Angol\tFaerchiril is at Barad Angol. Himeirion has asked you to tell the Elf-scholar Faerchiril about your findings in Sâd Doldúr.\n",
[11293]="70071605\n1\tBurn the afflicted saplings (total: 9)\tBurn the afflicted saplings near Shádhag. Shádhag can be found north-west of Sormedân.\n2\tReturn to Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân\tReturn to Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân with the report of your success.\n",
[11294]="7005467E\n1\tHelp Damrod with 'Clear the Path'\tDamrod has asked that you assist the Rangers in Zhar Dushgoi. You should complete 'Clear a Path' to help the Rangers in the Circle of Wrath.\n2\tFind Dorgam\tDorgam and Dolenthol ventured into the fortifications to the east to gather more information about the Orcs. You should search for Dorgam and discover what he has learned.\n3\tHelp Dorgam with 'Weaken the Barricades'\tDorgam has asked that you assist the Rangers in Zhar Dushgoi. You should complete 'Weaken the Barricades' to help the Rangers in the Circle of Wrath.\n4\tFind Dolenthol\tDorgam has sent you ahead to locate and assist Dolenthol in the Circle of Wrath. You should find Dolenthol.\n5\tHelp Dolenthol with 'Orders from Above'\030Help Dolenthol with 'Thin the Ranks'\030Help Dolenthol with 'A Hasty Escape'\tDolenthol requires your aid in completing several tasks while deep behind enemy lines. You should complete quests to help the Rangers in the Circle of Wrath.\n6\tTalk to Dolenthol\tWith your tasks completed, you should return to Dolenthol.\n7\tTalk to Damrod\tDamrod can be found in Barad Angarth, in the Circle of Wrath. You should talk to Damrod and apprise him of the situation amongst Gothmog's Orcs.\n",
[11295]="700173C3\n1\tAssist Ossur with the trolls in the Grand Stair\030Assist Ossur with the Fire-orcs in the Grand Stair\030Assist Avar with the Moria Orcs in the Grand Stair\030Assist Thithrand with the Warg-riders in the Grand Stair\030Assist Thithrand with the White Hand Orcs in the Grand Stair\tAvar, Ossur, and Thithrand are at the Orc-watch. Avar has asked you to complete the several tasks needed to reclaim the Grand Stair before he sends you back to Narfi at the Twenty-first Hall.\n2\tTalk to Avar at the Orc-watch\tAvar is at the Orc-watch. The dwarves of the Orc-watch are satisfied that the forces of the Orcs within the Grand Stair no longer pose a threat to Lothlórien.\n",
[11296]="70041180\n1\tDraw forth and defeat the leader of the Dead in Tarlang's Crown\tThe leader of the Dead can be drawn forth by defeating many of the Dead in the main encampment in Tarlang's Crown. Gondren has asked you to seek out the leader of the Dead in Tarlang's Crown, hoping that it will weaken the alliance between the Dead and the Heirs of Castamir.\n2\tTalk to Harnion\tHarnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas. You have defeated the oathbreaker, Nerzus, for a third time and weakened Azruthor's hold on Tarlang's Crown. You should now return to Harnion.\n",
})
